{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes","id":620572,"title":"4th edition changes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-08T15:00:37-07:00","id":620572,"title":"4th edition changes","content":"Given WtA is right after VtM, this might be typical in few years.<br /> <br /> One change I wish;<br /> <br /> -Retool some of the tribes.<br /> As in, Red Talons, Stargazers and Wendigo being the most in dire need of remodeling. We can argue all day about whether these need it, but just by looking at any MUSHs/Forum's/Chat's banned tribes list, these three are there. Children of Gaia also need some retooling, as they are based solely on a 20th century human ideal. And this tribe is supposed to be old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T18:00:07-07:00","id":620760,"title":"","content":"While this might strike some as too close to Forsaken, perhaps W4 can ease up on concerns over breeding, namely the result of two Changers of the same type. Hand in hand with this, reword the first tenet and make Kinfolk slightly more powerful. Whether or not these changes happen, though, I think it may be time to rename the metis. The ahi set a much more evocative standard, so perhaps each breed should have a different name for their equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:12:56-07:00","id":620933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=620760#post620760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this might strike some as too close to Forsaken, perhaps W4 can ease up on concerns over breeding, namely the result of two Changers of the same type. Hand in hand with this, reword the first tenet and make Kinfolk slightly more powerful. Whether or not these changes happen, though, I think it may be time to rename the metis. The ahi set a much more evocative standard, so perhaps each breed should have a different name for their equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least the rename would be good, given the word's meaning outside WtA.<br /> <br /> As for more radical changes, I'm kind of half-way. Forsaken's no-werewolf-mating was more grandfathered from WtA than anything, many games I've seen have dropped it and the game runs just fine without it. In WtA, the role and place of a metis is -much- more important and relevant to the game.<br /> <br /> Then again, some retooling would be good in all three breeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:19:36-07:00","id":620934,"title":"","content":"Before we can really start talking about W4th, I think we really need to wait to see just what thematic changes V4th goes through. It may give it some ideas as to just how far they want to go with re-naming, re-identifying, re-branding, and re-imagining aspects of the game lines.<br /> <br /> HOPEFULLY any mechanical changes they make will take the other fat splats into consideration, so maybe there's some discussion publicly that can/should be done for balance/setting, but then again, while many players DO combine games, they all take place in their own slivers of the CWoD, unlike NWoD which is meant to all be played together.<br /> <br /> So, as for mechanical changes, it's really going to depend on the path V4th takes.<br /> As for broader strokes like renaming forms, re-imagining Tribes, and the likes, we'll just have to see how far they're willing to change Clans first, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, since Rich recently posted that 4th Edition just happens to be around the time of the 25th anniversary and isn't guaranteed to be released in 2016, it could be two years before we see V4th released, so this thread may be pretty outdated and forgotten by the time W4th comes along. :-/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:32:58-07:00","id":620941,"title":"","content":"No matter how far ahead, the announcement just stirred up too much energy. I know I had hopes for more changes than W20's nature would allow, and the implications of V4 brought the idly wonderings back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T00:35:28-07:00","id":620963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=620941#post620941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter how far ahead, the announcement just stirred up too much energy. I know I had hopes for more changes than W20's nature would allow, and the implications of V4 brought the idly wonderings back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto.<br /> <br /> And given the developers look at this forum, seeing what people wish might give them ideas what to change. And given the vast changes we've seen done for Forsaken and Requiem yet the games surviving intact, there is hope that bigger changes won't ruin the game.<br /> <br /> A lot of the tribes do need some touching up, not many as most are actually pretty solid to this day. And maybe Skin-Dancers get edited as well. BSDs were all ready remade for W20, so I don't think they need it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T13:10:33-07:00","id":621573,"title":"","content":"To see the Skin-Dancers already with enough spiritual back-up to actually work as a tribe would be interesting, even if not an easy path for play.<br /> <br /> I would LOVE to see the Nation a little less biased on everything else, so you don't have to keep such a low profile when you actually do a cross-over. I know the ancient enmity between weres and vamps is a classic one, but I got tired of it. Even in a weres-only game it limits too much the possibilities of the game. Limits to: you break everything with Wyrm-taint or you become Ronin. That's kinda lame...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T15:19:32-07:00","id":621659,"title":"","content":"The changes i want are:<br /> <br /> 1) Get rid of Purebreed as a mechanic because its badly designed. It replaces the need for social stats and as it is a background it makes 0 sense for not taking five. And while one can argue that it only works against werewolves and kin, garou society is so separated that it makes they are the only people PC will interact mostly.<br /> IMO it should only be relevant to reproduction or as a prerequisite to certains tribes and nothing else.<br /> <br /> 2) Get rid of the shapeshifting roll. It was never a good idea, even in novels when it happened it didnt add &quot;drama&quot; it just makes me wonder why noone turns around, slaps the guy and takes his werewolf card from him.<br /> <br /> 3) Give the forms purpose. They did the same wonderful thing in forsaken, i would like to make forms relevant. While Forsaken werewolves are hunters and all the forms are geared towards the &quot;hunt&quot;, in WtA werewolves are warriors and i would like all the forms geared towards that role.<br /> <br /> 4) Get rid of damage rolls. The secuence of &quot;attack roll-&gt;damage roll-&gt;then soaking rolls&quot; is pretty bad. I makes situations in which a PC does an awesome attack roll and a meh damage roll. It takes from the fun of the game and the more logical one would be &quot;attack roll-&gt;defense roll-&gt;soaking roll&quot;<br /> <br /> 5) Make regeneration simpler. The whole you cannot heal in breed form is an unecesary extra book keeping<br /> <br /> 6) Rebalance gift camps entirely. Remove the specific gifts from Silver Fangs houses and make them avaible to all the tribe. They already have lodges and frankly some of the houses are umplayable like the indian house. Give the camps like the inminent strike something special because its the most &quot;player friendly&quot; camp of the cogs and gives you nothing even though they are dies ultimate with a cog paint.<br /> <br /> 7) If they remove the Stargazer, please make kalindo avaible for everyone. Its nothing so special that any werewolf with a little martial training cannot figure it out.<br /> <br /> 8) Clarify what background go from 1 to 5 and which ones from 1 to 10 or 20. Like Zhyzhak having 20 points in totem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-09-2015, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T21:17:56-07:00","id":621862,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately Loki a lot of what you want is anathema to classic werewolf. I think the only change I agree with is the shapeshifting roll. <br /> <br /> Combat can be smoothed out a great deal but my concern would be the resulting lack of power behind attacks that garou are known for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T21:47:56-07:00","id":621869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=621862#post621862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately Loki a lot of what you want is anathema to classic werewolf. I think the only change I agree with is the shapeshifting roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that most of them other than completely getting rid of the shapeshifting roll could actually be fit into a modified frame that's still very much recognizably W:tA. Pure Breed, for example, can be handled the way that the EX3 developers mentioned they were changing the Breeding Background - you have a single grade of it that adds to social roles, and that's it. There's no need for more bred than thou mechanics beyond that. Now if only we could get some sensible changes on Vampire's end and trash the &quot;drinking blood from werewolves with PB gives you mad bonuses!&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> They should get mad bonuses from drinking hsien blood, like the other vampires do.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of Silver Fang special faction Gifts did get turned into general Silver Fang Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combat can be smoothed out a great deal but my concern would be the resulting lack of power behind attacks that garou are known for. </div> </div> </div>That depends on how you structure the unrolled damage. Strength would probably figure into it quite prominently, and if you make weapon damage count for levels instead of dice, Razor Claws becomes frighteningly effective. In fact, you'd probably need to buff Killing Bite for the Rokea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T22:31:27-07:00","id":621896,"title":"","content":"Regarding <b>Pure Breed: </b><br /> I agree that Pure Breed seems odd that it is &quot;My Tribal Purebreed&quot;, yet it acts as a &quot;Universal Garou Purebreed&quot;. <br /> I'd like to see Pure Breed be effective for YOUR Tribe, but have little, or no effect on other Tribes. In the canon, every Tribe claims that &quot;'They' may have higher pure breeding, but we don't think much of those dirty dogs&quot;, but mechanically even the Glass Walkers, who have abandoned the pure breeding among themselves, are somehow slaves to the power of it in others.<br /> <br /> <b>Glass Walkers: </b><br /> It seems like any major storyline involving the Glass Walkers eventually moves to the Tribe evolving again into the next stage.<br /> Technology has moved beyond the cities. Even remote villages in the depths of Africa have cell phones and Facebook pages, and Bitcoin and digital currency are being traded around the globe, so if the Tribe is following the technology and changes in culture into cyber-ether, then follow that path... take the tools that the Humans are playing with and adapt those things into new tools against the Wyrm. Sure there will be a strong presence in the cities, but the evolution from the 80s and 90s is beyond the money markets and into technological incubators and monolithic tech companies. Of all of the Tribes, the Glass Walkers are ready for a change because they evolve with the human race's growth, for better or worse. Maybe it's even time for them, or another camp to take one step closer to becoming Weaver-tainted?<br /> <br /> <b>Declaration Phase:</b><br /> Get rid of it, or just make it optional. I've never had a game (in ANY system that used it) that lasted more than one round of the Declaration phase. I get why it makes sense (why give those who rolled worst the opportunity to effectively &quot;hold their action&quot; until everyone has gone without any mechanical penalties, other than not having a target to hit, or having been hit/disrupted before their turn?), but it's cumbersome to remember what you said you were going to do, and for an ST to remember as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Ancestors/Past Life:</b><br /> Even after all of these years, how it works, what it truly represents, and how players and STs can use it tends to still be a bit muddy. Maybe it's been clarified somewhere in all respects, but it just hasn't sunk in with me and folks I play with. ^.^<br /> <br /> <b>Fera:</b><br /> Okay, a minor bit, but it's always been a bit weird that the werebears are GINORMOUS when they're in war-form, but a weretiger isn't much bigger than a werewolf. I get that the Garou are &quot;designed by Gaia to be the warriors&quot;, and thus their size and strength should be bigger, but the Garou's strength comes in packs. A Khan should be 14+ feet tall, IMO, with higher strength and dexterity. Their claws and teeth should naturally be more deadly too (Note: I get that their Chatro/Hispo form are their War-Form, but let's be realistic... few players play it that way and it doesn't make that much sense.) Again, I don't think that the balance should be 1-on-1, but a pack against a Khan... 5 Garou on 1 Simba/Khan/Gurahl/etc., should be in the Garou's favor, and why they wiped the earth nearly clean of the other Fera.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the War of Rage, are the Fera still going to be a (mostly) enemy of the Garou, or are we going to make them uneasy allies/partners in the setting? We already have at least two organizations where the Fera and Garou work together (Ahadi and Beast Courts), so with the times changing and the way most players/STs running their games, is it time to make an uneasy truce among the shifters in the final days of the fight in 4th Edition?<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Tactics:</b><br /> MOAR. Seriously. Working as a pack in combat should be HIGHLY encouraged, and doing so with more mechanical advantages should be part of the combat system. Add more official &quot;pack tactics&quot; in the book, or add some generalized bonuses based on the number of the Pack doing the same attack, or something. &quot;We're using Pack Tactic 20&quot; and having each Garou have both the bonuses to the combat round, as well as any negatives, might be a great option. Again, pack tactics should be something that each Pack should work on and be taught. Maybe each Tribe has their own tactics they specialize in, or bonuses when dealing with their favored enemy, or using their favored weapon, or <i>&quot;If 3, or more Get are fighting a Bane in a round, all allied combatants get a +1 die to attacks against that Bane that round.&quot; </i>Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T23:05:47-07:00","id":621912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=621896#post621896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Fera:</b><br /> Okay, a minor bit, but it's always been a bit weird that the werebears are GINORMOUS when they're in war-form, but a weretiger isn't much bigger than a werewolf. I get that the Garou are &quot;designed by Gaia to be the warriors&quot;, and thus their size and strength should be bigger, but the Garou's strength comes in packs. A Khan should be 14+ feet tall, IMO, with higher strength and dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength, yes. Dexterity, no. They're lucky to have the same Dexterity bonus as the Garou if they're verging on Gurahl Crinos size. Their Stamina would also be relatively low, because cats hit for power and not endurance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their claws and teeth should naturally be more deadly too (Note: I get that their Chatro/Hispo form are their War-Form, but let's be realistic... few players play it that way and it doesn't make that much sense.) Again, I don't think that the balance should be 1-on-1, but a pack against a Khan... 5 Garou on 1 Simba/Khan/Gurahl/etc., should be in the Garou's favor, and why they wiped the earth nearly clean of the other Fera. </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Gurahl, it was also the difference in Rage. The Deadly Hugbear could crush one member of a pack, but the rest would tear into him, never to give out hellish war-embraces ever again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of the War of Rage, are the Fera still going to be a (mostly) enemy of the Garou, or are we going to make them uneasy allies/partners in the setting? We already have at least two organizations where the Fera and Garou work together (Ahadi and Beast Courts), so with the times changing and the way most players/STs running their games, is it time to make an uneasy truce among the shifters in the final days of the fight in 4th Edition? </div> </div> </div>If they're going on course for the metaplot, there should be an uneasy partnership. Also, the Beast Courts should be rubbing elbows with the Garou Nation with great frequency, as well as not seen as unusual in that they exist and have a long history of their own apart from the Garou Nation. The &quot;east is east and west is west and never shall the twain meet&quot; crap needs to go into the trash can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T05:28:37-07:00","id":622073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=621862#post621862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately Loki a lot of what you want is anathema to classic werewolf. I think the only change I agree with is the shapeshifting roll.<br /> <br /> Combat can be smoothed out a great deal but my concern would be the resulting lack of power behind attacks that garou are known for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I get the whole Kalindo for everyone (but thats is considering they remove the stargazer) and the camps because......<br /> <br /> How is making galbro relevant being an anathema to classic werewolf?<br /> <br /> And getting rid of damage rolls would actually make garou attack more powerful. You do an good attack roll and the net hits of that would be added automatic damage base on Strength/weapon.<br /> <br /> Making regeneration/weakness to silver universal to all form would remove iffy rules like, only kin can forge Klaives because they made of silver. Why? In breed form, silver suposedly doesnt do anything and silver smith arent on the habit of burning themselves with silver if they know their craft but no, only kin folk can forge klaives because........<br /> <br /> Or to more general examples of very convoluted rules. Garous in all forms except in their breed can soak aggravated except if said damage is in silver then they cant but then in their breed form silver doesnt do anything. But they cannot regenerate in their breed form but if they fall unconsious they can......its just a convoluted mess that is simplify by saying &quot;silver does aggravated damage to all forms, aggravated can be soaked by all forms and rengeration happens in all forms&quot; while at the same time helping the notion that homids are different from humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-10-2015, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:07:15-07:00","id":622096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=621862#post621862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately Loki a lot of what you want is anathema to classic werewolf. I think the only change I agree with is the shapeshifting roll.<br /> <br /> Combat can be smoothed out a great deal but my concern would be the resulting lack of power behind attacks that garou are known for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would be. Just because -we- are used to the clunky mechanics, doesn't mean they are good. We just are used to them. If real changes are to happen, stuff needs to be cleaned with a hedgetrimmer.<br /> <br /> For example, the aformentioned Pure Breed. I've played WtA for years and with PB characters, and if there is any stat in WtA that is unneededly complicated, PB is it.What it is varies so much from book to book, that you can get into legimate flamewars about it in-game. W20 has the best definition for PB by far, it is tribe specific, you can't keep it and switch tribes. Simple, right? But yet, I've seen so many people complain about it, even though the only situation where it would matter would be a tribe switching PC.<br /> <br /> I personally think Spirit Heritage should be lifted as an equally important stat, if not combined into PB. And both should be treated as more a general stat without dot ratings. You either have it or you don't, no 1-5.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the more general soak rolls would be easier to remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:13:50-07:00","id":622103,"title":"","content":"Kailindo for everyone DOES make sense, simply because it is the <b>freaking stated goal</b> of the Star Gazers to spread Kailindo over the tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:42:47-07:00","id":622156,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Pure Breed being most effective within the tribe, but I think that it should also be effective with different tribes. Perhaps 1/2 as effective with historical neighbors and a quarter with others.<br /> <br /> Garou and human interaction less face facts the average Ahroun can not blend into society very easily this is not a bad thing but plays hell with having a character that wants to have a job of some sort. The ability to work means resources, and unless you're going to create a multi-national company that provides a stipend to packs this creates a wealth of problems. <br /> Ancestors/Past Lives clarify what it does, characters that channel an ancestor should also probably be given a social bonus within the Tribe. Eliminate some of the tribal background bans. I can see the loss of mystical backgrounds or even physical ones in some cases. But not every tribe needs to have restrictions on Allies, contacts, resources, etc. Yes Bone Gnawers are the bottom of society in the Garou Nation but this should be reflected in a social penalty in interaction with other tribes not oh you are so poor you eat soup cans and if this is the case then give the Gnawers a stronger social network poor people in the real world develop strong social networks usually among families that aid each other. This could be done by requiring Bone Gnawers to have 3 dots in either Allies or Kinfolk. <br /> I have no problems or little problem with most of the combat mechanics I did away with the whole declare actions thing years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:47:17-07:00","id":622158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=622156#post622156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou and human interaction less face facts the average Ahroun can not blend into society very easily this is not a bad thing but plays hell with having a character that wants to have a job of some sort. The ability to work means resources, and unless you're going to create a multi-national company that provides a stipend to packs this creates a wealth of problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a system all ready, it's called kinfolk. Kinfolk make most of the money in most tribes, and through that money garou can have a decent living.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:30:11-07:00","id":622237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=622103#post622103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kailindo for everyone DOES make sense, simply because it is the <b>freaking stated goal</b> of the Star Gazers to spread Kailindo over the tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or because it's not exactly a complicated and intricate problem for any given werewolf to realize that they can dodge more easily if they shrink down into a smaller form, change mid-punch to catch someone off-guard with a longer arm, etc. Shapeshifting tricks should be an everyday affair for a group of shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, while dividing powers into Charms and Knacks didn't work for Lunars, it might work out for Garou and Fera to have shapeshifting refinement powers separate from normal Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T09:41:33-07:00","id":623380,"title":"","content":"I find that the Pure Breed is something that should work on every garou. But the bonus to social rolles is mechanically a broken system. In our LARP we made every even Pure Breed dot a bonus on Willpower to protect against gifts that are socially (Persuation-based, Domination-based, or the like), while only ever uneven dot granted a bonus on such gifts.<br /> <br /> For, being a paragon of your tribe doesn't only mean that you can scare the shit out of other garou, but also means you don't bow down to a bone-grawer, who happens to roll Intimidate on you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T09:42:51-07:00","id":623386,"title":"","content":"Oh, while Vampire IV is an advance into the 21th century, I hope that not too much is changed setting-wise. I kind of like most of the WtA Setting, while mechanics often suck...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T13:53:36-07:00","id":623646,"title":"","content":"The problem is what to do with the Apocalypse. If it is post-pone, it downplays the previous setting. If it already occurred, we NEED significant changes to bring the point of it being the world after the Apocalypse. Or, again, it will downplay the very event that is so important to the game that it gives it its name and defines how the Garou Nation organizes itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T14:16:48-07:00","id":623654,"title":"","content":"I would argue, that the Apocalypse did not happen. If it had happened, it wouldn't be cWoD anymore - it would be WoD-Deadlands or something.<br /> <br /> The garou have been worried about the Apocalypse for some hundred years, if it didn't happen in the last 20 years, maybe it is all going to happen in the near future.<br /> I mean, if one just ignores that the signs of Phoenix already happened, one is fine. Ignore the no true born cubs, which is in any way redundant, since W20 tells us, you can't determine a baby as garou or kin by simple gift usage anymore.<br /> <br /> We play Werewolf LARP in 2015 and will still be playing in 2030 - we don't need an Apocalypse simply because that is the name of the game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T15:11:21-07:00","id":623684,"title":"","content":"So I've been following this for a bit, and I wasn't quite sure what I'd like to see changed for 4th. I think having the world set in a post-apocalypse (if at all possible) would be an interesting spin. If not possible it's definitely a source book I'd love to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T15:53:04-07:00","id":623727,"title":"","content":"Or perhaps the Apocalypse is happening and it's not one sudden fight that's done in a day, but it's a conflict that itself takes years to resolve....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T16:07:03-07:00","id":623732,"title":"","content":"What if the signs for the Apocolpyse were wrong and it was discovered that it was much further into the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T18:03:07-07:00","id":623825,"title":"","content":"I find oddly enough that the Apocalypse in.....werewolf the apocalypse is no as prevalent as gehenna in vampire. I think thats because in vampire you are a few years away from it (player 90/2000) and lots of signs are pointing to it while in Apocalypse the feeling would be the same whether you playing in 90/2000 or in the wildwest, its always coming.<br /> <br /> Also because in a way, you know how vampire apocalypse is more specific. Its has its own special name (gehena) and the short version is &quot;antideluvian rise up, and eat our faces&quot;. While werewolf is just &quot;the apocalypse&quot; not much more than that, even the feel is that is not gonna be a big cataclismic thing, just the garou loosing and loosing ground until they die off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T22:10:58-07:00","id":623925,"title":"","content":"The Mage: the Ascension Revised Convention Books were (as best as I read) an interesting setting.<br /> For the Mages, Time of Judgement came... and went. Yes, Umbral Storm hit, and the Void Engineers are fucked up with most of their bases lost and those who can navagate through the storm that still rages come back with some crazy tales and war stories.<br /> Meanwhile, for everyone else, things got shaken up... but the world didn't end, but many of the factions are still recovering.<br /> <br /> There's a brief mention of the Werewolves and the Vampires, saying that &quot;For them, their end times came and... nothing happened.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, this could mean a few things:<br /> 1) In the CWoD setting, the Apocalypse/Gehenna were adverted (somehow) with the results mitigated in such a way that the Mages just aren't aware of the cosmic evidence/happenings.<br /> 2) The Time of Judgement actually SPLIT the spheres of the CWoD into their own realms, completely severing the influence of one over the other (the CWoD games had the ability to, but weren't really designed to be played together, and their production/development was not intended to be balanced/influenced by the themes/balance of the others. It was like different roads that SOMETIMES crossed, or ran alongside each other briefly, but never merged truly into one unified highway system.) The paradigms just aren't that compatible as one main, flawless setting.<br /> <br /> It will be interesting to see how V4 handles the timeline and greater CWoD as a setting. :-/<br /> <br /> However, for Werewolf, the End Times certainly felt more massive than they did for Vampire. In Werewolf, we weren't talking about powerful figures rising up and bringing the end, but rather the fabric of the universe being squeezed and rotted until everything finally gives way and existence is rent asunder in a physical and spiritual way. We may very well be IN the churning, grinding Apocalypse, like falling into a black hole. The very idea that the Garou are fighting to prevent a thing that is already happening is part of the great story for me--they fight a losing battle because it is their duty, it is their destiny, and it is the Good and Right thing to do. Those who succumb to the fact that it's a lost battle and they have already lost either become lost to depression, or turn to the other side to join the &quot;winning&quot; side and enjoy the view as the world burns down around them--why fight it?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">And the band played on<br /> As the helicopters whirred<br /> Drunk on the lawn in a nuclear dawn<br /> My senses finally blurred<br /> <br /> --Moxy Fruvous &quot;The Drinking Song&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just my two cents. Your mileage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T02:59:20-07:00","id":624032,"title":"","content":"The Avatar Storm of Revised isn't the end times for Mage, it is actually covered in the book &quot;Ascension&quot;. And it turns all of humanity into full-fledged Mages. Some Mages saw the Storm as the Time of Judgement, but truly it was just the Week of Nightmares saying &quot;hello&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not to say that it isn't a valid interpretation for the end times to have no major impact. But...<br /> <br /> In Werewolf it DOES have a major impact one way or another. Their society is defined by prophecy and by the war. Even putting the Apocalypse in the future, without outright ignoring Revised Era will have an impact because of so much prophecies and things happening around without the expected consequences.<br /> <br /> Just for the record: vamps aren't the only ones with their own name to the end of times. Actually, as far as I remember the Fera are the only ones to call it Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:45:44-07:00","id":624320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=624032#post624032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Avatar Storm of Revised isn't the end times for Mage, it is actually covered in the book &quot;Ascension&quot;. And it turns all of humanity into full-fledged Mages. Some Mages saw the Storm as the Time of Judgement, but truly it was just the Week of Nightmares saying &quot;hello&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not to say that it isn't a valid interpretation for the end times to have no major impact. But...<br /> <br /> In Werewolf it DOES have a major impact one way or another. Their society is defined by prophecy and by the war. Even putting the Apocalypse in the future, without outright ignoring Revised Era will have an impact because of so much prophecies and things happening around without the expected consequences.<br /> <br /> Just for the record: vamps aren't the only ones with their own name to the end of times. Actually, as far as I remember the Fera are the only ones to call it Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>NB: Fera is the word that the Garou use to refer to other shapeshifters, not the word for all shapeshifters. The closest you get to one like that is the Rokea word Changer (they don't refer to other Changers with a special word, either). Otherwise, you're dealing with Bete, Killi, Khurah, Ovid, and any number of other terms.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Fera, though, the Mokole and Rokea don't share the fatalism of some of the younger Changers. The former recall the WonderWork of the Dissolver and previous unmaking of the world. The former are meant to survive and don't see anything as the end times, only the might be end times or the end times for everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T10:33:00-07:00","id":624466,"title":"","content":"1: First Change at any age. I was tired of playing a teenager when I still was a teenager.<br /> <br /> 2: Camps that break tribal\u200bl boundaries. The Valkyries recruiting females from other Tribes, Crows recruiting whomever they need from wherever they need them.<br /> <br /> 3: Stargazers as less of 'leaving the nation' and more as a bridge to the Courts<br /> <br /> 4: Ahadi guide shortly after. Maybe a new Hengeyoki guide as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T14:31:02-07:00","id":624648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=624466#post624466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: First Change at any age. I was tired of playing a teenager when I still was a teenager.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Although the possibility of Lunatics was kind of forgotten in revised, it seemed. Would be nice if they would return them with some prominence, but also allow for some middle-aged garou to have a normal late First Change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=624466#post624466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: Camps that break tribal\u200bl boundaries. The Valkyries recruiting females from other Tribes, Crows recruiting whomever they need from wherever they need them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within reason. For some Camps it makes sense, but for others not so much. Crows for example still kind of serve the tribe and possibly should manipulate or force others for the benefit of the tribe, not invite them in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=624466#post624466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3: Stargazers as less of 'leaving the nation' and more as a bridge to the Courts</div> </div> </div> </div>I would leave that open to the STs. I find their current state, with some Stargazers living amongst the garou (or as hermits in the western world) and with some living amongst themselves, and some amongst the Best Courts okay.<br /> The Best Courts for the most part don't want or need contact to the garou in the west and therefore establishing the Stargazers as a bridge seems wrong.<br /> But also, the &quot;they have left&quot;-statement was unnecessary, for their Elders ordered them to return to their home territory and that is certainly within their right and the Litany - so the other tribes should not blame anything on any Stargazer who did his duty and went there, and neither blame anything on a Stargazer who's personal responsibilities made him stay.<br /> It's not like the tribe declared themselves Ronin and abandoned Gaia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=624466#post624466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4: Ahadi guide shortly after. Maybe a new Hengeyoki guide as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T01:24:42-07:00","id":625217,"title":"","content":"It really would be nice to drop the notion of East and West being entirely different settings as if they weren't even in the same planet.<br /> <br /> Didn't knew Fera was just for other shapechangers, and actually we use it as all-inclusive in my group. So I will keep it that way for personal use, makes more sense to me, and is simpler and shorter than shapechangers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:22:27-07:00","id":625600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=624466#post624466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: First Change at any age. I was tired of playing a teenager when I still was a teenager.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this actually can lead to a bigger change and question. It seems pretty silly, but one of the biggest issues I've seen in online games crop up is related to this.<br /> <br /> Can garou have jobs? Do they live at the Caern solely? Are kinfolk their sole providers? What is the role of kinfolk?<br /> <br /> And to us veterans, the answer to all of those questions is yes. But what I've seen online, I do think they should be reconsidered at least a bit. If players want characters who are financially independent and live separate from the caern, maybe that should be considered to be made more possible.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, one of the biggest problems with players doing this with their characters, is that the role for kinfolk lessens. If the garou are all ready doing what the kin are supposed to, it leaves the kinfolk PCs with basically a servant role and a role as breeding stock. Most end up being solely the latter, and it can get disturbing. They all ready changed how Wolf-Blooded are done in WtFv2, so changes are coming.<br /> <br /> I'd like at least some thought put into this, as I do think a lot of players just don't like having characters as moochers. But then again kinfolk should not solely be servants and breeding stock.<br /> <br /> Another thing that crops up with late changes, is how it affects Metis or Lupus. Do they just naturally get earlier changes than homids?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:23:27-07:00","id":625741,"title":"","content":"I think that early First Changes (&lt;17 in general) only seem to work well if you also play character staying as cubs for years. Otherwise it's super awkward. Also tying First Change age to rage rating (and therefore auspice) doesn't really work too well, because you keep winding up with 13-year-old Ahrouns running around and no, just no.<br /> <br /> It's seemed to work alright to say that the First Change is brought out by stressful situations, and the bar gets lower as they get older...so Garou in third world hellholes full of child soldiers are going to wind up changing in like the 11-14 range because of all the constant life or death situations, someone in America in their mid teens might shift when an abusive parent beats them, and someone with a nice cozy life might get by until they get mugged...or when they get fired from their job due to some nasty office politics. Clearly there can be advantages to the Garou forcing a shift, with a nice fun balance between &quot;don't traumatize the kid when they're pretty young&quot; vs &quot;maybe they'll hit some event in life where they just snap before you get around to it&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Added plus is daydreaming for your players that have really cushy lives. 'What if I'm really Garou but I don't know it because my life never sucked that bad? Whooaaah.')<br /> <br /> Aren't Metis normally supposed to shift somewhere around 8-11, and Lupus around 1-2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:30:00-07:00","id":625744,"title":"","content":"i really wish they go with the forsaken route on that. <br /> <br /> &quot;First change comes normally during puberty, not always. handwave it away&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:34:20-07:00","id":625746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625741#post625741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that early First Changes (&lt;17 in general) only seem to work well if you also play character staying as cubs for years. Otherwise it's super awkward. Also tying First Change age to rage rating (and therefore auspice) doesn't really work too well, because you keep winding up with 13-year-old Ahrouns running around and no, just no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of assumed they do? The basic cliath is 'round 15-19 years old, after years of training in combat and tribal culture. Lupus especially would need a year at least to learn all the tips and tricks in a non-Talon sept. Metis' RoP is possibly hard to earn, so they'd be older just by the time it takes them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:39:08-07:00","id":625748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625217#post625217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really would be nice to drop the notion of East and West being entirely different settings as if they weren't even in the same planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like that. I mean, sure for game set in India, Himalayan or other regions that are bordering on the territory controlled by the Beast Courts of the Emerald Mother there would be a grey area as to how one would interact. But besides that, every continent has its unique flavour, I guess, and that is okay.<br /> <br /> Garou, and most Shapechangers, are essentially territorial and I kind of dislike the whole &quot;global gaia brotherhood&quot;. Local septs and their neighbour septs should be the focus of game play, unless you want the pack to travel around, but then each place they get to should be new and exciting and in no way the same as everywhere.<br /> <br /> So, having Africa, South America, Australia and the far East being different from the North American/European standard is really fine with me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:16:13-07:00","id":625787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625600#post625600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this actually can lead to a bigger change and question. It seems pretty silly, but one of the biggest issues I've seen in online games crop up is related to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the same argument every once in a while, but I usually convince others of my point of view...<br /> So my answers (how I see it and would like to have it kept in the Setting):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625600#post625600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can garou have jobs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of.<br /> First, they can surely learn a job pre-first change. I would argue, that doing so would require their Rage score to be low. But the Curse probably isn't fully active pre-first change, so interacting with humans and animals still would work reasonably well for any late-bloomer garou.<br /> <br /> After the first change I'd say, that it depends on the job in question and the Rage trait in general. I liked the rules about having a human life that were in 2nd Edition tied to a roll, but were scrapped and turned into a solely ST responsibility in revised and W20.<br /> <br /> That said, if older Characters are allowed to have a first change, they probably would still only get character creation points to spend. A neonate also does get only a fixed amount, regardless of age and abilities directly prior to the Embrace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625600#post625600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they live at the Caern solely?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Garou do not necessarily live on caerns. They have pack territories. These are in the protectorate, the area the sept feels responsible for, that is outside the caern bawn. If a caern is a holy place, like a church, then the garou are like the congregation. The congregation doesn't usually live in or adjacent to the church. The priest and his family might. Same goes for caerns, in my opinion. Sure, some septs might be exceptions to the rule, but in general, garou packs have their own home turf and if you aren't the warder or one of the guardians, you only come to the caern if you have business there.<br /> <br /> And the hunting grounds of packs don't border on each other. There is a need to expand, evolve, move the territory if need arises. One doesn't want to tip-toe around other pack territories all the time. Think of gang turfs in cities, only that is here applies to stretches of land in a more rural environment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625600#post625600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are kinfolk their sole providers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. While garou should be always able to follow an Elders (or his pack alpha's) call to protect Gaia and probably do something to protect gaia even when no supernatural threat is currently known, they might generate income still. And there are the spoils of war: Fomori Pimps and Drug dealers have cash and a dead Pentex manager might not need his Benz or Rolex, so &quot;hello, Pawn shop&quot;.<br /> <br /> All in all, Garou can possibly fend for themselves, of they need to, but sure, the Kinfolk does help, as they are usually able to hold down stable jobs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625600#post625600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the role of kinfolk?</div> </div> </div> </div>I go with the PGtGG, which has the only Out-of-Character description of a &quot;ordinary&quot; kinfolk life (it is Children of Gaia, and other tribes might flavour it differently, but it is meant to be exemplary, and it is out-of-character, so it is the best source).<br /> <br /> Sure, there is a difference on what the garou see as the kinfolk's role and what the kinfolk would like his role was, but that is another topic, and probably one that generates personal drama in certain character-driven arcs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625600#post625600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to us veterans, the answer to all of those questions is yes. But what I've seen online, I do think they should be reconsidered at least a bit. If players want characters who are financially independent and live separate from the caern, maybe that should be considered to be made more possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>One can have Resources 5 and one can never bother to go to the caern to participate in Moots. But that brings it's own problems. I mean, one can be a Ronin or part of a community. If one wants to live in the garou community that is a sept, there are certain duties required.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625600#post625600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, one of the biggest problems with players doing this with their characters, is that the role for kinfolk lessens. If the garou are all ready doing what the kin are supposed to, it leaves the kinfolk PCs with basically a servant role and a role as breeding stock. Most end up being solely the latter, and it can get disturbing. They all ready changed how Wolf-Blooded are done in WtFv2, so changes are coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But, maybe that is a problem of it's own.<br /> Kinfolk can do stuff only kin can do, garou can do stuff they don't take the kin with them, when they do, and vampires don't work in sunlight. My point being: If you play garou, have all players garou. If you play Kin, do so in an all-kin campaign. If you mix, you will either be required to take the back-seat when the kin does her thing, or she will have to be just observer when the focus is on the garou part of thing.<br /> But, unless you appreciate the time the game focuses on the another player, this game will always suck. Especially, if the ST has halve the game time for one Kin and the other half for three+ garou players.<br /> <br /> Best way to avoid such problems is to not mix garou and kin, or have every player have two characters, so no part of the game session is unevenly distributed amongst players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625600#post625600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that crops up with late changes, is how it affects Metis or Lupus. Do they just naturally get earlier changes than homids?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could appreciate character concepts of Metis who had to be in Crinos till they were in their (human) fourties. Also, lupus, who change for the first time and have the body of a mid-thirties guy.<br /> <br /> Would require some minor changes in society, though, for they would surely start to train a Metis who is mature enough to act as a cliath, and probably send him on a Rite of Passage, since all his Regeneration and other powers are already active, just shapechangeing is not...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:27:26-07:00","id":625803,"title":"","content":"Other changes I'd like to see: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Loose the Rage, Gnosis and Willpower tie to the Auspice, Breed and tribe. There were so many nice other methods here in the forum, on how any of these choices would contribute to all three stats. Like Homid bringing +0 Rage, +0 Gnosis but +3 Willpower and Fianna bringing +2 Rage, +1 Willpower and +2 Gnosis and so on. That is, if the character creation remains the way it is, which brings me to my next point...</li> <li>Change the character creation. Have Building Points, that are equivalent to XP. Have one free dot in each trait, that has a minimum of 1 point (like Willpower, attributes, or Vampire virtues), all other traits are 0. Then spend the experience to make the character, just as you would advance him. Sure, Backgrounds and Merits/Flaws would need Experience Point costs for such a character creation, but why not. Just state, they only are viable during character creation or make them an optional system to acquire Backgrounds and Mertis/Flaws in game with Experience. We use a system like that (aided by php/mysql/javascript) to handle characters for our (non-MET) LARP for several years now, and it works fine. Such a system would work well for the complete classic WoD and make different splats more comparable, experience wise.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T14:46:57-07:00","id":625947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625748#post625748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like that. I mean, sure for game set in India, Himalayan or other regions that are bordering on the territory controlled by the Beast Courts of the Emerald Mother there would be a grey area as to how one would interact. But besides that, every continent has its unique flavour, I guess, and that is okay.<br /> <br /> Garou, and most Shapechangers, are essentially territorial and I kind of dislike the whole &quot;global gaia brotherhood&quot;. Local septs and their neighbour septs should be the focus of game play, unless you want the pack to travel around, but then each place they get to should be new and exciting and in no way the same as everywhere.<br /> <br /> So, having Africa, South America, Australia and the far East being different from the North American/European standard is really fine with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking abou they being equal. I talk about them having no impact upon each other. Nothing against most Fera not wanting to deal with other territories, and surely I can see these places having distinct cultures and ways of handling things.<br /> <br /> But it is another thing entirely to just treat as if they where another world completely, and most of the time that's the feeling. Even natural rules seem to change from West to East.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:12:58-07:00","id":625974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625787#post625787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Garou do not necessarily live on caerns. They have pack territories. These are in the protectorate, the area the sept feels responsible for, that is outside the caern bawn. If a caern is a holy place, like a church, then the garou are like the congregation. The congregation doesn't usually live in or adjacent to the church. The priest and his family might. Same goes for caerns, in my opinion. Sure, some septs might be exceptions to the rule, but in general, garou packs have their own home turf and if you aren't the warder or one of the guardians, you only come to the caern if you have business there.<br /> <br /> And the hunting grounds of packs don't border on each other. There is a need to expand, evolve, move the territory if need arises. One doesn't want to tip-toe around other pack territories all the time. Think of gang turfs in cities, only that is here applies to stretches of land in a more rural environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why I think it needs clarification, because from my experience has been that pack territories are part of the Bawn of the Caern. And obviously the ternal question is, where the metis cubs go? Sure, canon states that some are raised in basements, but as many are said to live on Caern grounds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625787#post625787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But, maybe that is a problem of it's own.<br /> Kinfolk can do stuff only kin can do, garou can do stuff they don't take the kin with them, when they do, and vampires don't work in sunlight. My point being: If you play garou, have all players garou. If you play Kin, do so in an all-kin campaign. If you mix, you will either be required to take the back-seat when the kin does her thing, or she will have to be just observer when the focus is on the garou part of thing.<br /> But, unless you appreciate the time the game focuses on the another player, this game will always suck. Especially, if the ST has halve the game time for one Kin and the other half for three+ garou players.<br /> <br /> Best way to avoid such problems is to not mix garou and kin, or have every player have two characters, so no part of the game session is unevenly distributed amongst players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, in these situations the games were online forum games, with RP going on 24/7. Yet, the kinfolk still ended up being little more than breeding stock. While there have been some great ones, most still were kinda of useless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625787#post625787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could appreciate character concepts of Metis who had to be in Crinos till they were in their (human) fourties. Also, lupus, who change for the first time and have the body of a mid-thirties guy.<br /> <br /> Would require some minor changes in society, though, for they would surely start to train a Metis who is mature enough to act as a cliath, and probably send him on a Rite of Passage, since all his Regeneration and other powers are already active, just shapechangeing is not...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like that idea, but then there is the problem of the Veil. Do packs then just leave metis at the Caern for every city trip? What about a city Caern, how would it deal with the metis that hasn't changed?<br /> <br /> In a lot of ways, the early change for metis is also useful in terms of their usability and veil-safety.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:07:33-07:00","id":626026,"title":"","content":"One change I wish:<br /> the authors actually proofread the text for contradictions before releasing it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:24:57-07:00","id":626034,"title":"","content":"Oh there's a thing. Contradictions specifically in the rules. Like forsakens wolf gift cost on release. One said 2 points another said something else. Yay for charts.<br /> <br /> On the matter of stats, what if they went with the new world of darkness route and tied stats to, well stats? Like stamina + size = hp. <br /> <br /> The problem with this is it fundamentally changes a few mechanics and I would understand them not going that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:06:29-07:00","id":626089,"title":"","content":"Well, health and damage mechanics DO need to fundamentally change anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T19:20:31-07:00","id":626149,"title":"","content":"1. I've run Werewolf since second edition, and have had characters that played every conceivable concept under the sun. I have never played or run a game on line and will not discount the experience of others. Kinfolk as a background gives you a family perhaps an estranged one but a family. I have never had a player say hey I'm going to call my sister Becky and hit her up for the cash we need to rent a car. I have had a character whose family owned a cleaning service that didn't mind helping with those pesky blood stains and letting characters take the place of a cleaning crew. I have had a character whose brother was an EMT and could provide emergency first aid. <br /> 2. Not every Garou is going to live at the Caern it is not possible or realistic Garou will need to go into public and I doubt many Caerns have showers. Further if a Caern is attacked from a tactical stand point it makes sense that a few packs would be held in reserve or off site to attack the attackers from behind. I can see the Elders plus family living at a Caern. A few packs living in scattered areas around the Caern and even a few that actually live within the Bawn. <br /> 3. Garou holding jobs is possible especially since Glasswalkers tend to live in cities and many Caerns that are given as examples are in office buildings. <br /> 4. Garou probably go through 4-8 years of training it takes time to build skills before a rite of passage and part of that would include certain lessons for lupus and merits characters. Further given that it is almost impossible in North America or Europe to get a job without a GED or a High School education and given the Rage of the average Ahroun I could see home schooling being used to help protect the Veil. Remember that the whole range of Child advocates will target under age characters. My city is not alone in having a curfew for persons under 18 and nothing screams Veil breech faster than a cop stopping a minor for breaking curfew only to have said cop ripped to shreds.<br /> 4. Late change Garou can work but unless the pack is at least 18+ or appears that way this can lead to another set of problems see child advocates above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T02:52:29-07:00","id":626458,"title":"","content":"The point isn't if things work that way on the setting. It is that it isn't clear on the books. It could, should even, be clearer stated and talked about at a somewhat greater length.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T05:09:22-07:00","id":626492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=626458#post626458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point isn't if things work that way on the setting. It is that it isn't clear on the books. It could, should even, be clearer stated and talked about at a somewhat greater length.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. As much as freedom of expression is great, having a clear baseline would be better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:21:27-07:00","id":626661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625947#post625947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it is another thing entirely to just treat as if they where another world completely, and most of the time that's the feeling. Even natural rules seem to change from West to East.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think this is a production flaw. Meaning authors of one book probably didn't have enough information on Settings like Rage Across Australia or KotE to really write about them in their tribe books, and so they ignored them mainly...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:33:29-07:00","id":626667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625974#post625974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is why I think it needs clarification, because from my experience has been that pack territories are part of the Bawn of the Caern. And obviously the ternal question is, where the metis cubs go? Sure, canon states that some are raised in basements, but as many are said to live on Caern grounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pack territories aren't listed amongst the stuff that is on caern bawns, in sourcebooks that detail these, like Guardians of the Cearns.<br /> <br /> Yes, Metis are probably raised amongst garou, depending on who has to raise them. W20's Rage Across the World leaves this questionable honour to the Father/Mother of the Den (who in contradiction to other sources therefore can't be Kin). Older sources like Fianna 1st state that nobody will foster a Metis, so the parents are forced to do so (implying, they aren't executed for their crime).<br /> In any case, if the Den Father/Mother isn't also the Warder or a Guardian, she and her pack might have their own pack territory, and it probably has to be suitable for Metis raising, if the sept feels this is part of the office's duties. If the sept gathers at the caern, the metis cub probably has to come to the sept, too - for you won't find a babysitter for the metis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625974#post625974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, in these situations the games were online forum games, with RP going on 24/7. Yet, the kinfolk still ended up being little more than breeding stock. While there have been some great ones, most still were kinda of useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see - but my argument might still work. Have STs forbid the garou to do certain things and have players have secondary kin characters (from their Kinfolk and Allies backgrounds) to do that stuff instead.<br /> The only hard thing is to find a consensus on what garou can do with a certain Rage score, and what not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=625974#post625974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like that idea, but then there is the problem of the Veil. Do packs then just leave metis at the Caern for every city trip? What about a city Caern, how would it deal with the metis that hasn't changed?<br /> <br /> In a lot of ways, the early change for metis is also useful in terms of their usability and veil-safety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but that is a problem that really only arises if someone wants to play a late-first-change Metis.<br /> And I think the argument was, not to have all First Changes later in live, but to have the option to have them later.<br /> <br /> And really, I would like to have more Lunatics-elements back in Werewolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:37:03-07:00","id":626669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=626026#post626026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One change I wish:<br /> the authors actually proofread the text for contradictions before releasing it</div> </div> </div> </div>Or change stuff after the texts are discussed before in the forum. That said, I'd like more open development and possibility to give feedback while the book is written. The time window before the PoD goes online is usually to short for me to read the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:38:31-07:00","id":626670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=626034#post626034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the matter of stats, what if they went with the new world of darkness route and tied stats to, well stats? Like stamina + size = hp.<br /> The problem with this is it fundamentally changes a few mechanics and I would understand them not going that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too, and especially the Healthlevel tied to size and stamina was something I liked a lot.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:47:36-07:00","id":626738,"title":"","content":"I kind of wish tghey would allow for more homid rokea, I like the Rokea, but I would like to see more Homid. As IIRC rokea hate their homid born kin and kill them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T11:05:59-07:00","id":626748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=626738#post626738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of wish tghey would allow for more homid rokea, I like the Rokea, but I would like to see more Homid. As IIRC rokea hate their homid born kin and kill them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>They typically kill the kinfolk before they can get together with another Rokea to make one born to humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T11:47:19-07:00","id":626760,"title":"","content":"By default, Rokea are completely unplayable unless the game is Rokea-only or is about being constantly hunted by the Rokea society. And with their society, there aren't even much things to go for in the ocean except constant hack'n'slash. One of the most interesting splats among the Fera, and the single least enjoyable to play.<br /> <br /> And that makes almost no sense. Why, for the sake of the gods, do they hate dry land so much!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:19:10-07:00","id":626786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=626760#post626760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default, Rokea are completely unplayable unless the game is Rokea-only or is about being constantly hunted by the Rokea society. And with their society, there aren't even much things to go for in the ocean except constant hack'n'slash. One of the most interesting splats among the Fera, and the single least enjoyable to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you need to do is make it explicit in the text that putting the focus on things beside the Betweener War is okay, just like with Werewolf games that don't involve subsidiaries of Pentex or other WICs, or the war in the Amazon. Taking manageable pieces of the giant for your own use should be the directive of putting games together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that makes almost no sense. Why, for the sake of the gods, do they hate dry land so much!? </div> </div> </div>Turna'a. Half of all of the Rokea got blown up in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Wigwam\" target=\"_blank\">Operation Wigwam test</a>, which also produced the Balefire Sharks and ruined a powerful undersea Caern. Having Rage, the Rokea are not inclined to leave that little detail alone, even if their unlimited lifespans give them a longer view than many other Changers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:57:33-07:00","id":626841,"title":"","content":"Rage and extra actions. Is it not a little striking that the <i>fastest </i>changing breed can never be faster than 5 extra actions in a turn--AND, that being able to take those five turns requires that one's rage be so high that they're functionally a ticking bomb (absent constant use of rage/anger/what-have-you management gifts and meditation, etc.)? What sort of grinds my gears about it is that vampires--literally every vampire--has the capacity to achieve the same degree of speed, regardless of generation (albeit, those with the Celerity in clan will invariably get there faster, cheaper).<br /> <br /> Really, for me it's not that five extra actions aren't enough--it's that five extra actions is only possible if you're walking the absolute razor's edge of sanity (unless you also have Willpower 10 and Gnosis 10--in which case, well done), but it's an otherwise impressive, but unremarkable feat for certain other supernaturals. I'm thinking that there's a better way (probably).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:14:34-07:00","id":626872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan;n621896<br /> [B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fera:[/B]<br /> Okay, a minor bit, but it's always been a bit weird that the werebears are GINORMOUS when they're in war-form, but a weretiger isn't much bigger than a werewolf. I get that the Garou are &quot;designed by Gaia to be the warriors&quot;, and thus their size and strength should be bigger, but the Garou's strength comes in packs. A Khan should be 14+ feet tall, IMO, with higher strength and dexterity. T[/I]Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always thought it's just absurd the size changes that shapeshifting makes for werewolves in the game, given that the average wolf is somewhat smaller than the average human. Make them faster and stronger than either humans or wolves due to supernatural power, yes, but a towering 9'+ wolf man seems very out of place to someone who grew up on <i>An American Werewolf in London</i> and <i>The Howling</i>.<br /> <br /> Tigers can get upwards of 600 lbs., so make the intermediate forms scale up in size from human to full tiger. Ditto with bears, which can easily weigh over a half ton and don't really need any enlargement to be terrifyingly powerful animals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:17:39-07:00","id":626966,"title":"","content":"Even with Operation Wigwam test, it is just too much of a stretch to assume such a hate for everything linked to the dry land.<br /> <br /> Werewolves should be the ultimate warriors of Gaia and not even they are so insanely full of Rage. It is Impergium + War of Rage on steroids.<br /> <br /> Also pretty much stupidity for a splat meant to survive. Y'know, such a fury makes you <u>very</u> prone to put yourself in danger, and end up dead.<br /> <br /> I think Rank could enhance the extra actions gained from Rage. Better yet, it should define your limit on Rage usage instead of Dexterity and Half your Perm Rage.<br /> <br /> Not going as far as to say that it is easy for any vamp to accomplish the same, it is actually easier for the Fera. BUT, indeed, it could at least have ways to do so without so much drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:27:56-07:00","id":626971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=626966#post626966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with Operation Wigwam test, it is just too much of a stretch to assume such a hate for everything linked to the dry land.<br /> <br /> Werewolves should be the ultimate warriors of Gaia and not even they are so insanely full of Rage. It is Impergium + War of Rage on steroids.<br /> <br /> Also pretty much stupidity for a splat meant to survive. Y'know, such a fury makes you <u>very</u> prone to put yourself in danger, and end up dead.<br /> <br /> I think Rank could enhance the extra actions gained from Rage. Better yet, it should define your limit on Rage usage instead of Dexterity and Half your Perm Rage.<br /> <br /> Not going as far as to say that it is easy for any vamp to accomplish the same, it is actually easier for the Fera. BUT, indeed, it could at least have ways to do so without so much drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rokea lost half of everyone they knew in one attack. As Bleeds-Night noted in the breedbook, if 3 or 4 billion humans just suddenly died, the remainder would get pretty strange, too. Besides, they're still pragmatic when they operate on the surface and don't seek to just wreck shit willy nilly; per the Sins of Sharks short story, they tend to be extremely, even bizarrely, surgical. On a metatextual level, the Rokea have their reason for being imperiled internally just like every other breed. Conflict and problems abound to make for stories of struggle, not hard restrictions.<br /> <br /> (I generally do feel that Rokea need their frenzy trigger point shifted from two successes to four or more; only certain types of sharks would have it at two, and they aren't the ones that most people might think)<br /> <br /> As for Rank and Rage, it shouldn't be built into any power stat's function beyond its improvement to self-control and aid in holding off frenzies. Similarly, I feel that making Tick Body grant Ananasi extra blood point storage based on Rank was a blunder that needs to be changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:32:22-07:00","id":627052,"title":"","content":"The extra actions rules from the Celerity in Dark Ages 20 are pretty good, in my opinion. I'd like to see Rage actions limited in some fashion, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:48:31-07:00","id":627055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=627052#post627052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The extra actions rules from the Celerity in Dark Ages 20 are pretty good, in my opinion. I'd like to see Rage actions limited in some fashion, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that limiting them in the same fashion would be a good move. Garou and Fera are meant to be murder machines, whereas vampires simply move quickly when they use blood. Unlike vampires, Changers have to be under a good deal of stress to use their super-speed, and it tends to overwhelmingly skew toward responding to the source of said stress. Maybe if the mechanics just get evened out instead of having mountains and valleys of character capability, it will work a bit better.<br /> <br /> Gurahl Rage can also result in the essential certainty of popping someone's skull like a grape (20+ dice to grapple and deal damage for several turns!), so there's that to balance against, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-14-2015, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:52:00-07:00","id":627057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=626971#post626971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Rokea lost half of everyone they knew in one attack. As Bleeds-Night noted in the breedbook, if 3 or 4 billion humans just suddenly died, the remainder would get pretty strange, too. Besides, they're still pragmatic when they operate on the surface and don't seek to just wreck shit willy nilly; per the Sins of Sharks short story, they tend to be extremely, even bizarrely, surgical. On a metatextual level, the Rokea have their reason for being imperiled internally just like every other breed. Conflict and problems abound to make for stories of struggle, not hard restrictions.<br /> <br /> (I generally do feel that Rokea need their frenzy trigger point shifted from two successes to four or more; only certain types of sharks would have it at two, and they aren't the ones that most people might think)<br /> <br /> As for Rank and Rage, it shouldn't be built into any power stat's function beyond its improvement to self-control and aid in holding off frenzies. Similarly, I feel that making Tick Body grant Ananasi extra blood point storage based on Rank was a blunder that needs to be changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The very idea of half their population lost in one attack is ludicrous to begin with, on several levels. And given their longevity, they should have a better grasp of things than that. They are the single most savage Changing Breed for no reason except being influenced by bad shark movies.<br /> <br /> And even that isn't really relevant. What is relevant is that you have less possibilities for playing a Rokea, or even using it as an NPC, than you have with any other Fera. Period.<br /> <br /> Extra actions for Fera are a tricky question. In truth, I think the system should get rid of Extra Actions once and for all. But if not, we have something here at once too easy and too costly.<br /> <br /> Resources-wise, the Fera got an easy time with Extra Actions. I mean, to say that any vampire can get the same number of E-A isn't an argument, such a vampire spent a helluva lot of resource to do so. To build Rage straight to 10 is a lot easier. Indeed, you have access to Extra Actions to begin with without even buying Rage. And to use that, you spend Rage Points, nothing so hard to recover (if it would Gnosis, them we would have a problem). Indeed, some builds can guarantee that you never exhaust your Rage, and they aren't harder to get than Celerity 5 for a vampire.<br /> <br /> But them we have the main problem with Rage: Frenzy. That's the real prob, because you can't have 5 extra actions without risking frenzy for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Stopping again to think about it, Rank indeed isn't the best way to handle Extra Actions, but half your Rage shouldn't be, either. Assuming most of the rules remain the same, maybe they could just drop the &quot;half your Rage&quot; limit and put &quot;five&quot; in place. Simpler and more feasible without turning your character into walking nitroglycerin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T16:44:02-07:00","id":627112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=627057#post627057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very idea of half their population lost in one attack is ludicrous to begin with, on several levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet you don't bother to articulate why. Also, it wasn't an attack as such, though there are some conspiratorial whispers certain that it was. They were meeting at a grotto, and the world was moving on without them in a dangerous way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And given their longevity, they should have a better grasp of things than that. They are the single most savage Changing Breed for no reason except being influenced by bad shark movies. </div> </div> </div>No, the Garou are the most savage, bar none. The Rokea simply have an oversight in Rage successes and a long history of having cooler heads than the time after they experienced nuclear testing (along with its concomitant massive casualties to their numbers), along with industrialized fishing, oil spills, and islands of garbage. Their view, like the Zhong Lung, is so long that they can miss an awful lot if another Changer type doesn't stop by to bring news and yet another breed isn't there to rouse them to action. They have this baggage because they don't have any baggage from the War of Rage, and they were required some source of internal conflict.<br /> <br /> It could be dialed back a bit, and given that a new whole edition picking off from the last metaplot bits of Werewolf would have to deal with Mateo's existence, we'd probably get something a bit different. Pity about the Ceilican, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T21:08:00-07:00","id":627218,"title":"","content":"No, I didn't bothered in the least to articulate why, and I won't. That's because it would derail the topic. As I said, it doesn't really mater if their backstory is enough to explain their status quo or if it is, as I said, ludicrous. What does mater is that said status quo, explained or not, made them the least useful of the Fera.<br /> <br /> I do like the concept of the Rokea, and the idea of exploring the sea in a game about any of the Fera. But as their description goes, there aren't much avenues for such a game. Some, true, but not as many as we could have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:29:45-07:00","id":627857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=627055#post627055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that limiting them in the same fashion would be a good move. Garou and Fera are meant to be murder machines, whereas vampires simply move quickly when they use blood. Unlike vampires, Changers have to be under a good deal of stress to use their super-speed, and it tends to overwhelmingly skew toward responding to the source of said stress. Maybe if the mechanics just get evened out instead of having mountains and valleys of character capability, it will work a bit better.<br /> <br /> Gurahl Rage can also result in the essential certainty of popping someone's skull like a grape (20+ dice to grapple and deal damage for several turns!), so there's that to balance against, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I pride myself to have made the suggestion that the Rage spend by Gurahl should at least have a duration of several turns, to be half-way balanced.<br /> <br /> In any case, no bonus in the WoD can currently compare to an extra action. No &quot;soak gift&quot;, certainly not Fortitude or the Gurahl way of spending Rage. I mean, a garou shifts and has at least 5 dots strength + weapon damage he gets to reuse, if the scores only one success on an attack that usually the enemy has no action do dodge anymore - and that for 1 Rage. Even with &quot;Razor Claws&quot; massively pimped in W20, the bonus isn't really comparable.<br /> <br /> The extra action is certainly the most powerful thing a character could get in combat - and that is true for basically every system there is (and I played many). To limit the attack actions per round should certainly be part of a revamping of the combat system. And I hope that comes.<br /> <br /> And I like the suggestion someone made here or in the other topic, that one should use the Shadowrun-Way: Attack-&gt;Dodge/Parry-&gt;Soak. And that damage is a fixed value, depending on Strength, weapon, active gifts and so on, but not a dice roll.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T21:20:30-07:00","id":629542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=627857#post627857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I pride myself to have made the suggestion that the Rage spend by Gurahl should at least have a duration of several turns, to be half-way balanced.<br /> <br /> In any case, no bonus in the WoD can currently compare to an extra action. No &quot;soak gift&quot;, certainly not Fortitude or the Gurahl way of spending Rage. I mean, a garou shifts and has at least 5 dots strength + weapon damage he gets to reuse, if the scores only one success on an attack that usually the enemy has no action do dodge anymore - and that for 1 Rage. Even with &quot;Razor Claws&quot; massively pimped in W20, the bonus isn't really comparable.</div> </div> </div> </div>In retrospect, Razor Claws could have indeed done with a bit more, yes. A few Gifts are still not really quite as impressive as they could be, and I fully believe that first levels should be impressive, because a number of Fera get what Garou would have to work for at earlier ranks, sometimes even right out of the gate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The extra action is certainly the most powerful thing a character could get in combat - and that is true for basically every system there is (and I played many). To limit the attack actions per round should certainly be part of a revamping of the combat system. And I hope that comes.<br /> <br /> And I like the suggestion someone made here or in the other topic, that one should use the Shadowrun-Way: Attack-&gt;Dodge/Parry-&gt;Soak. And that damage is a fixed value, depending on Strength, weapon, active gifts and so on, but not a dice roll.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Well, other than the attack roll's net successes, anyway. Those stage the damage up/increase the number of boxes done, depending on which edition of SR you're talking about. Though, if multiple attacks have to get abstracted to avoid being too effective, even that might not be left intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T22:34:25-07:00","id":629568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=629542#post629542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, other than the attack roll's net successes, anyway. Those stage the damage up/increase the number of boxes done, depending on which edition of SR you're talking about. Though, if multiple attacks have to get abstracted to avoid being too effective, even that might not be left intact.</div> </div> </div> </div>When i did that suggestion i was reffering to 5ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T00:40:10-07:00","id":629670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=629542#post629542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In retrospect, Razor Claws could have indeed done with a bit more, yes. A few Gifts are still not really quite as impressive as they could be, and I fully believe that first levels should be impressive, because a number of Fera get what Garou would have to work for at earlier ranks, sometimes even right out of the gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that there shouldn't be ever more damage or power added. It is time to dial it down a notch, or three, or five.<br /> I mean event the thought of &quot;Razor Claws is to weak, for an extra action is way more effective, so lets pimp Razor Claws&quot; was ill conceived for it doesn't address the fact that multiple actions are too powerful, and makes all the other bonus damage gifts that didn't make it into W20 look even more useless...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T09:54:54-07:00","id":629994,"title":"","content":"Damage have to be severely tuned down, and/or health tuned up. Extra Actions have to be thrown out ASAP, in all its current forms, for a modern system where different kinds of actions can happen in a turn, but not different stances of the same action.<br /> <br /> With that, we can finally change the rules on damage types. The current rules only serve to make Aggravated Damage default instead of something to be feared, and Stamina a crappy, useless, attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T16:34:03-07:00","id":630393,"title":"","content":"How so. Stamina allows to soak agg damage, if you are a werewolf and it is 50% of the soak gift activation roll (for Luna's Armour, Troll Skin, Steel Fur). I personally, find it okay, that garou often deal with agg damage and therefore need some time to heal. If one uses VtM or what ever to crossover, agg seems powerful for they can't soak in within their rule systems. But in this cases I'd always go with the rules of Possessed (agg soak with 0 dice, half stamina or full stamina - depending on how combat oriented the NPC is).<br /> <br /> Health levels = Size + Stamina (as per nWoD) would also be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:26:38-07:00","id":635097,"title":"","content":"Other changes I'd make:<br /> - Rename Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies to Uncontrollable frenzies. There should be some ambiguity in whether or not Rage is of the Wyrm, not a blatant statement in the mechanics. The potential for cannibalism and ultraviolence can stay, but the rape and necrophilia are things that can turn people who would otherwise be interested in savage horror away, particularly since oversexed violence has become a terrible cliche in an awful lot of media.<br /> - Simplify Animal Attraction into just adding Primal-Urge to your seduction, carousing, and befriending rolls unless the subject would be seriously uninterested. I seriously just don't see the need to add in a complicated subsystem for it, and don't think it needs to be a sex beam. If you want iffy ethical quandries, pick up the Kitsune Gift Seduction, or use Persuasion, to say nothing of the myriad <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EItka8KXeq0\" target=\"_blank\">influence Gifts that Galliards get</a>.<br /> - Reduce Gift costs in chargen to 3, 4, or 5 bonus points, depending on whether it's in-splat, one of those general Beast Courts picks, or outside of splat, respectively.<br /> - Increase the cultural spread on tribes. The Fianna, Bunyip, and Croatan can stay as more regional tribes, but the rest should have coverage on par with all of the Silver Fang houses. This can also help to alleviate a lot of the &quot;shitloads of European tribes, just a few everywhere else&quot;, and removes the burden of &quot;Asian tribe&quot; from the Stargazers. Also, it's entirely possible to have more than just Silent Striders with jackal read African wolf heritage, so you can bring a lot of the tribes all the way down to sub-Saharan Africa.<br /> - Have Black Furies be as open to transwomen as the M20 Sisters of Hippolyta. If you want them to be more savage about it, take a page from the langsuir of the Golden Courts. But only just one page, because there are a lot of Devil-Tigers there.<br /> - Don't refer to Hispo as a dire wolf. Ditto for Bastet, their Chatro form, and Sabertooths, as well as Rokea, Chasmus/Fighting Jaws, and the megalodon (<a href=\"http://www.elasmo-research.org/education/evolution/megalodon_as_sandtiger.htm\" target=\"_blank\">it's very likely not what you thought it was</a>).<br /> - Rename the Children of the Dire (and Song of the Dire) or ship them over to the Uktena as a Camp that's close to the Nuwisha (dire wolves were a sister species to coyotes).<br /> - Don't make Ananasi, Ratkin, Mokole and others have to get Gifts to have near-human and/or near-beast forms. Just put them in right off the bat, so that we can get cool five-fold spread artwork for everyone.<br /> - Build in rules that can handle huger-than-Gurahl Mokole forms, or don't bother and keep the hugeness to Dream Semblance.<br /> - Unrolled defense like in post-1e Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=630393#post630393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so. Stamina allows to soak agg damage, if you are a werewolf and it is 50% of the soak gift activation roll (for Luna's Armour, Troll Skin, Steel Fur). I personally, find it okay, that garou often deal with agg damage and therefore need some time to heal. If one uses VtM or what ever to crossover, agg seems powerful for they can't soak in within their rule systems. But in this cases I'd always go with the rules of Possessed (agg soak with 0 dice, half stamina or full stamina - depending on how combat oriented the NPC is).<br /> <br /> Health levels = Size + Stamina (as per nWoD) would also be greatly appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>cWoD does soak as a matter of course, nWoD uses Stamina to get extra health levels, so we're unlikely to see the latter even if the former isn't quite what we get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T16:03:35-07:00","id":635118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=635097#post635097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other changes I'd make:<br /> - Rename Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies to Uncontrollable frenzies. There should be some ambiguity in whether or not Rage is of the Wyrm, not a blatant statement in the mechanics. The potential for cannibalism and ultraviolence can stay, but the rape and necrophilia are things that can turn people who would otherwise be interested in savage horror away, particularly since oversexed violence has become a terrible cliche in an awful lot of media.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, pretty much. There are people who power through thralls, but to some that kills the character in all but literally.<br /> <br /> That, and after the conversation about cannibalism we had here, I do think it being more tied to the character truly losing themselves works better. Also, yes, the rape part is rather..yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T16:48:58-07:00","id":635133,"title":"","content":"Yeah, going to have to agree on those frenzies. I know a whole lot of people who just plain aren't willing to play a Metis of rage 6+, especially on MUSHes where you really have to live with your character. Though if you keep distinct homid/lupus uncontrollable frenzies, then what do you give the metis to replace them? I could see self-mutilation working thematically but it would be too likely lethal. I guess there's no real need to have breed specialties there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2214,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","user":"Traveller","date":". 08-24-2015, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T16:53:24-07:00","id":635144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=635133#post635133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, going to have to agree on those frenzies. I know a whole lot of people who just plain aren't willing to play a Metis of rage 4+, especially on MUSHes where you really have to live with your character. Though if you keep distinct homid/lupus uncontrollable frenzies, then what do you give the metis to replace them? I could see self-mutilation working thematically but it would be too likely lethal. I guess there's no real need to have breed specialties there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking either player's choice or trigger circumstances. Or it might just be all cannibalism, all the time, since it leads to a litany violation and standing over a fallen foe and turning him into a bunch of unidentifiable pieces isn't really different enough from a normal frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T22:34:28-07:00","id":635452,"title":"","content":"Actually, has thrall actually had an impact of purpose in games much? Other than punishing high Rage characters, it seems rather tacked on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T23:21:19-07:00","id":635477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=635452#post635452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, has thrall actually had an impact of purpose in games much? Other than punishing high Rage characters, it seems rather tacked on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to be there to ratchet up the personal horror factor. It wasn't there in first edition, though, and the correlation of the breeds to Triatic Wyrms seems to add to the tacked-on factor, because if it's true, then humans are all collectively tainted by the Eater-of-Souls, among other weird conclusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T02:05:59-07:00","id":635520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=635477#post635477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems to be there to ratchet up the personal horror factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it succeeds at that. Metis kill-raping whatever they can get their claws on is pretty horrific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T07:56:16-07:00","id":635809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=635520#post635520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it succeeds at that. Metis kill-raping whatever they can get their claws on is pretty horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's off enough from the events of combat that it just reminds me of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2WsAnORTxgI\" target=\"_blank\">a character from The Venture Brothers</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:18:18-07:00","id":635818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=635477#post635477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems to be there to ratchet up the personal horror factor. It wasn't there in first edition, though, and the correlation of the breeds to Triatic Wyrms seems to add to the tacked-on factor, because if it's true, then humans are all collectively tainted by the Eater-of-Souls, among other weird conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and as said before, since its name you basically have to assume your char got wyrmtainted. I think if it was mostly cannibalism and called something like 'Thrall of the Predator', it would give a sense of how bad garou frenzies can get that they forget even the littlest restraint. And, after playing in some general werewolf RPs where the common argument against WtA is that they aren't really werewolves, it could connect with the myth more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=635520#post635520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it succeeds at that. Metis kill-raping whatever they can get their claws on is pretty horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I have nothing against using rape in a story. Shit happens, bad shit especially. But as Traveler stated, it being tied to a player character means that people either don't dare to pick a high rage metis, or have to deal with the nasty reality of their character being a rapist. That tends to kill RP pretty quickly in online games.<br /> <br /> And then there is the fact that some people have legimate traumas, and bringing them up in play can be bad for them. Especially if its their character (after all, temp rage CAN get to 6).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T11:44:30-07:00","id":636118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=635818#post635818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly, I have nothing against using rape in a story. Shit happens, bad shit especially. But as Traveler stated, it being tied to a player character means that people either don't dare to pick a high rage metis, or have to deal with the nasty reality of their character being a rapist. That tends to kill RP pretty quickly in online games.<br /> <br /> And then there is the fact that some people have legimate traumas, and bringing them up in play can be bad for them. Especially if its their character (after all, temp rage CAN get to 6).</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything you said is true and I agree, rape can certainly serve a narrative purpose (just about anything can in the hands of a skilled storyteller).<br /> The worst part is your character is forced to do their best Reaver impression because of a crappy dice roll.<br /> <br /> Honestly, since the in-universe consequences of the Metis going out of control are so nasty, that might be a big part of the stigma attached to them. I could also see that as a compelling reason to make some fetishes that might restrain this tendency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T12:13:54-07:00","id":637251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=636118#post636118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything you said is true and I agree, rape can certainly serve a narrative purpose (just about anything can in the hands of a skilled storyteller).<br /> The worst part is your character is forced to do their best Reaver impression because of a crappy dice roll.<br /> <br /> Honestly, since the in-universe consequences of the Metis going out of control are so nasty, that might be a big part of the stigma attached to them. I could also see that as a compelling reason to make some fetishes that might restrain this tendency.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels like a kind of a cheap shot, like the whole of Caleb Davion from BattleTech. You thought that you were getting a true villain in the former white hat faction, but it was really someone in dire need of antipsychotics!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-23-2015, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T13:18:33-07:00","id":637317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=636118#post636118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, since the in-universe consequences of the Metis going out of control are so nasty, that might be a big part of the stigma attached to them. I could also see that as a compelling reason to make some fetishes that might restrain this tendency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. The majority of the stigma for metis comes from the fact that they not only are Litany breaches walking around, they are veil breaches that usually cost the Nation a warrior or two, they are sterile and so a genetic dead end to a dying race and they are always deformed in a significant way. I don't think the thrall needs to add to it.<br /> <br /> I honestly think any Thralling metis is just killed outright in most tribes, simply because the act was so horrific. And because its a metis, why should it be given any leeway?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T15:53:16-07:00","id":637490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=637251#post637251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That feels like a kind of a cheap shot, like the whole of Caleb Davion from BattleTech. You thought that you were getting a true villain in the former white hat faction, but it was really someone in dire need of antipsychotics!</div> </div> </div> </div>One man's villain is another's clinical patient. I don't see anything cheap there.<br /> <br /> Great reference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=637317#post637317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't agree. The majority of the stigma for metis comes from the fact that they not only are Litany breaches walking around, they are veil breaches that usually cost the Nation a warrior or two, they are sterile and so a genetic dead end to a dying race and they are always deformed in a significant way. I don't think the thrall needs to add to it.<br /> <br /> I honestly think any Thralling metis is just killed outright in most tribes, simply because the act was so horrific. And because its a metis, why should it be given any leeway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really like the 'sins of the father' angle on Metis. I am totally fine with prejudice, and laws against werewulf fucking, that is fine; but I want it to be justified, and the Thrall aspect adds a strong argument to hatred/distrust of the Metis. &quot;They occasionally go on crazy murderfucking rampages&quot; is a pretty good reason not to want to have to deal with them. Perhaps that is the sin of their creation being made manifest?<br /> <br /> On a semi related note, I have found it difficult to impress on my players why the Metis should be scorned. The afore-mentioned reasons are just nonstarters. And in my time period, Garou aren't quite on the brink of extinction. Yes, the Metis are hideous/weaker, and yes, they need to stay at the Caern for much of their lives. Still, most players respond with 'Mom and Dad fucked up and got their just desserts, so why should I shit on little Johnny Metis?' And the cannon NPC response is so unsympathetic and nasty. I feel like if I presented the Metis as being mistreated for existing I have to write a bunch of almost literal kick-the-dog moments. I don't enjoy having my entire Garou society act like assholes, and it is hard to foster any sort of sense of community or respect in a Caern when the crippled orphans are treated like whipping boys by the elders on down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 08-23-2015, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T21:21:16-07:00","id":637714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=621659#post621659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The changes i want are:<br /> <br /> 1) Get rid of Purebreed as a mechanic because its badly designed. It replaces the need for social stats and as it is a background it makes 0 sense for not taking five. And while one can argue that it only works against werewolves and kin, garou society is so separated that it makes they are the only people PC will interact mostly.<br /> IMO it should only be relevant to reproduction or as a prerequisite to certains tribes and nothing else.<br /> <br /> 3) Give the forms purpose. They did the same wonderful thing in forsaken, i would like to make forms relevant. While Forsaken werewolves are hunters and all the forms are geared towards the &quot;hunt&quot;, in WtA werewolves are warriors and i would like all the forms geared towards that role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure Breed doesn't replace the need for social stats; there are lots Gifts that rely on Social stats to be successful. And there are plenty of reasons that it doesn't make sense to just take 5 points in that background, first and foremost being that Werewolf isn't that kind of game. If you want to dominate others socially, there are much more effective ways than just min-maxing your backgrounds, and there is a lot of responsibility that comes with being a Pure Breed 5 Garou.<br /> <br /> I like your comment about forms though. New players can get confused about why there'd be any reason to use anything other than Homid, Crinos, and maybe the rare situational Lupus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T02:49:20-07:00","id":637808,"title":"","content":"Um. Hispo and Glabro are awesome? Why wouldn't you use them? Hispo is brilliant for combat and Glabro is the form you wear when you expect trouble and don't want to freak everyone out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T07:08:27-07:00","id":637980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=637808#post637808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um. Hispo and Glabro are awesome? Why wouldn't you use them? Hispo is brilliant for combat and Glabro is the form you wear when you expect trouble and don't want to freak everyone out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hispo has also always been the go-to form for jumping, since it gets you more air per success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T11:36:43-07:00","id":638236,"title":"","content":"For the purpose of thralls: Seems like one reason for them existing is to be a mechanical discouragement from taking extreme Rage. There's plenty of roleplay reasons to avoid it (or enjoy it), but even a hardened roll-player who wants ten Rage to beat things up faster needs something to fear, even if they stay away from social situations.<br /> <br /> Re: treatment of Metis. Maybe I'm extrapolating way too far, but Garou abuse of Metis serves a very useful purpose, even in tribes that don't think Metis deserve that kind of treatment: it gives one more reason not to make one in the first place. If Metis were well-treated then, okay, charaches can get killed for their crimes, but at least they have their love-child, and isn't that kinda worth it in a way? But if everyone likes to kick the Metis, then in addition to committing a great crime, you've brought someone into the world just to condemn them to a life of suffering. A Garou with true sympathy ought to do whatever they can to avoid bearing a Metis...and therefore, their own kind heart helps convince them to keep the Litany.<br /> <br /> Surely most Garou don't think of things in such terms, but Elders very well might (and it's the kind of thing that gets ingrained into society and kept because it works). If you reverse it, it's easy to argue that being nice to Metis starts making charaching not look so bad. Hell, look at religious fundamentalists' opposition to birth control or STD vaccinations: they're not dumb, they know more people get hurt, but if that fact helps scare others onto the straight-and-narrow then they figure it was worth it. Garou are, in their own way, very much fundamentalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T14:03:34-07:00","id":638331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=637808#post637808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um. Hispo and Glabro are awesome? Why wouldn't you use them? Hispo is brilliant for combat and Glabro is the form you wear when you expect trouble and don't want to freak everyone out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they are practically useless? Hispo is redundant as the &quot;combat form&quot; when there is crinos and Glabro is just there because of whole nonsense of not regenerating in breed form and writers cannot get on a consensus on how veil breaking it is. Some say you look like a particularly hairy men while other says you scream werewolf to the 4 winds.<br /> <br /> So if you are in a combat which veil isnt an issue why use galbro when Crinos, hispo or even lupus is avaible? If veil is an issue then galbro is also out depending on the mood of the writers. I really like glabro as a concept but in WtA is the redhead stepchild along with hispo. Except for jumping....i guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viking Funeral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=637714#post637714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure Breed doesn't replace the need for social stats; there are lots Gifts that rely on Social stats to be successful. And there are plenty of reasons that it doesn't make sense to just take 5 points in that background, first and foremost being that Werewolf isn't that kind of game. If you want to dominate others socially, there are much more effective ways than just min-maxing your backgrounds, and there is a lot of responsibility that comes with being a Pure Breed 5 Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup and those gift can also be stacked with Purebreed. And the problem with what you are saying is that the only defense for that mechanic is DM fiat or how he runs with it. As is written is given the player 3 to 5 dices for his social rolls for next to nothing point wise and the only drawback is &quot;other expect much of you&quot; which is kinda the normal for PCs for one and yes with 5 more dices to social rolls that character is gonna do a lot so its not really a drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T14:43:04-07:00","id":638366,"title":"","content":"Huh; I use hispo a ton for long-distance wilderness travel and for stealth missions where veil breaking also isn't an issue.<br /> <br /> Glabro...well, I guess it has the advantage where people can rationalize it as &quot;really really ugly guy&quot; _without_ supernatural influence, which means it's nice around WP10 folks. People might say you look like a monster, but not mean it literally. Sure, you stick out like a sore thumb to anyone with a dot of lore:werewolf, but you can rough up a mundane without much incident, and even be caught on camera without the newspapers saying &quot;werewolf&quot; in the morning. Yeah, regeneration is a veil breach, but if you do it in a dark alley people aren't going to think &quot;supernatural&quot;, they're going to think &quot;PCP&quot;. Also you can talk intelligibly, which is nice for hostile interrogations.<br /> <br /> Hispo is also useful in the same way for wolf-born. As long as you don't get caught on camera, and nobody studies your tracks, it's more reliably safe when you _need_ to get out of Lupus and risk a breach. It's not remotely perfect, but there are different degrees of veil breaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T15:36:31-07:00","id":638413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638366#post638366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh; I use hispo a ton for long-distance wilderness travel and for stealth missions where veil breaking also isn't an issue.<br /> <br /> Glabro...well, I guess it has the advantage where people can rationalize it as &quot;really really ugly guy&quot; _without_ supernatural influence, which means it's nice around WP10 folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that WP 10 people are rarer than werewolves? hell you cant really talk of them as folks they are, lack of a better phrase, &quot;dudes of legend&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638366#post638366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People might say you look like a monster, but not mean it literally. Sure, you stick out like a sore thumb to anyone with a dot of lore:werewolf, but you can rough up a mundane without much incident, and even be caught on camera without the newspapers saying &quot;werewolf&quot; in the morning. Yeah, regeneration is a veil breach, but if you do it in a dark alley people aren't going to think &quot;supernatural&quot;, they're going to think &quot;PCP&quot;. Also you can talk intelligibly, which is nice for hostile interrogations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not saying that regeneration is a veil breach (though it is), im saying that regeneration is needlesly complicated and silly. It would make more sense to regenerate in all forms really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638366#post638366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hispo is also useful in the same way for wolf-born. As long as you don't get caught on camera, and nobody studies your tracks, it's more reliably safe when you _need_ to get out of Lupus and risk a breach. It's not remotely perfect, but there are different degrees of veil breaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but this make no sense. Then Hispo is the purposeless form for the homids and galbro is the same for lupus and your example are depending on pretty rare/particular scenarios. <br /> <br /> Wouldnt it make more sense to make regeneration for all forms and give the hispo, galbro some advantage? Some purpose? Because i can really remove those 2 from the game as is written now and little would change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T18:37:12-07:00","id":638613,"title":"","content":"I've used all 5 forms in games I've played in.<br /> Homid for obvious human things<br /> Glabro in baggy clothes doesn't break the veil and allows you to go toe to toe with most non bad ass supernaturals. Also for fighting with guns/in gun fights.<br /> Crinos for serious combat while wielding weapons.<br /> Hispo for serious unarmed combat.<br /> Lupus for hunting and running down enemies/prey.<br /> <br /> All 5 forms have their purposes. It never occurred to me to just not use all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T18:56:14-07:00","id":638631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638613#post638613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glabro in baggy clothes doesn't break the veil and allows you to go toe to toe with most non bad ass supernaturals. Also for fighting with guns/in gun fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are going against a supernatural why not crinos? And i doubt Gaia though about guns when she made Garous. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638613#post638613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crinos for serious combat while wielding weapons.<br /> Hispo for serious unarmed combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a weapon that you can use in crinos, why bother in at all with unarmed? A vice versa if you have more point in unarmed why bother in crinos.<br /> <br /> Again, just saying they could use more integration with the setting/mechanics. As forsaken focused the forms towards the hunter, wta forms should be focused towards the warrior. The perks in Forsaken were great for that. The homid for hidding in the crowds, the glabro with its animal reflexes and to insolate prey and the hispo to drive the prey to the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:17:55-07:00","id":638691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638631#post638631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you are going against a supernatural why not crinos? And i doubt Gaia though about guns when she made Garous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Crinos isn't always an option. Glabro is good enough to kick the crap out of a few ghouls...in the middle of the street, or any other public space. And gun fights are a reality of the modern world, it doesn't matter if Gaia supposedly planned for it or not. I added that on as an afterthought, but it is still a use of Glabro. I am really just speaking from my personal experience with the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638631#post638631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you have a weapon that you can use in crinos, why bother in at all with unarmed? A vice versa if you have more point in unarmed why bother in crinos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which you have more points in shouldn't matter. You don't always have a choice. A greatsword is an awesome weapon to swing at an opponent who is vulnerable to it. Sometimes you get grappled, and armed combat isn't an option. Spirits can be immune to mundane weaponry and so claws (and fangs) are the only option you have that will work on them. It helps to be versatile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638631#post638631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Again, just saying they could use more integration with the setting/mechanics. As forsaken focused the forms towards the hunter, wta forms should be focused towards the warrior. The perks in Forsaken were great for that. The homid for hidding in the crowds, the glabro with its animal reflexes and to insolate prey and the hispo to drive the prey to the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never got into forsaken so I can't comment at all on how it works. I just know that I have used the various forms in WtA games. I don't know why they haven't worked out for you or your group, but in games I've played in I've used and seen others use the various forms for various situations.<br /> If you play WtA and the only forms you use are Homid and Crinos, I believe you maybe have not explored the setting enough. I'm not about to say you're playing it wrong or anything since it's a game and as long as people are having fun, you're doing it right. I just think maybe the various situations characters can get into haven't been explored enough.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:32:51-07:00","id":638704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638691#post638691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got into forsaken so I can't comment at all on how it works. I just know that I have used the various forms in WtA games. I don't know why they haven't worked out for you or your group, but in games I've played in I've used and seen others use the various forms for various situations.<br /> If you play WtA and the only forms you use are Homid and Crinos, I believe you maybe have not explored the setting enough. I'm not about to say you're playing it wrong or anything since it's a game and as long as people are having fun, you're doing it right. I just think maybe the various situations characters can get into haven't been explored enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on there, i never said i havent used them, i have used the full range of them but found very little use for hispo only for very very handful of occations if any. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T20:21:30-07:00","id":638731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638704#post638704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hold on there, i never said i havent used them, i have used the full range of them but found very little use for hispo only for very very handful of occations if any.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do apologize for inferring otherwise. No offense was intended. But yea, to each his/her own. I've found having access to the various forms to be quite useful for different situations. Hispo is quite a bit faster than every other form except Lupus. So it's really good for running down dangerous opponents. And it's arguably just as good (or superior) to Crinos for fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T21:20:05-07:00","id":638790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638413#post638413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realize that WP 10 people are rarer than werewolves? hell you cant really talk of them as folks they are, lack of a better phrase, &quot;dudes of legend&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite agree with your math there. According to the Delirium chart, WP 10 is 0.5% of the population, which is one per two-hundred. Garou and Fera number roughly one in two-hundred <i>thousand</i>, or even less favorably. There are literally at least a thousand people with WP 10 for every Changer. Admittedly, much of this can be chalked up to early-era WW not understanding numbers, but it's standing at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Im not saying that regeneration is a veil breach (though it is), im saying that regeneration is needlesly complicated and silly. It would make more sense to regenerate in all forms really. </div> </div> </div>Breed form is out because it's silver-safe, unless you're the breed that should formerly have been known* as metis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry but this make no sense. Then Hispo is the purposeless form for the homids and galbro is the same for lupus and your example are depending on pretty rare/particular scenarios.<br /> <br /> Wouldnt it make more sense to make regeneration for all forms and give the hispo, galbro some advantage? Some purpose? Because i can really remove those 2 from the game as is written now and little would change. </div> </div> </div>Some Gifts are actually keyed to work only in certain forms. Ancestral Wings is a Hispo-only affair, for example. You could build on themes along those lines.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Wow, future pluperfect conditional subjunctive!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T02:42:31-07:00","id":640014,"title":"","content":"In addition to the speed, bulk and athletics,if you're fighting with Fangs and Teeth, Hispo is the mathematically better choice then Crinos!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:31:12-07:00","id":640240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=640014#post640014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the speed, bulk and athletics,if you're fighting with Fangs and Teeth, Hispo is the mathematically better choice then Crinos!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Truth. I nerfed it my game since it felt like players were getting punished for using the 'war-form' for battle. I made Hispo grant less stamina, and rightly or wrongly that seemed to do the trick. Being faster and bitey-er is fine, but not without any trade-offs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 08-26-2015, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T09:23:26-07:00","id":640327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=640240#post640240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truth. I nerfed it my game since it felt like players were getting punished for using the 'war-form' for battle. I gave Hispo grant less stamina, and rightly or wrongly that seemed to do the trick. Being faster and bitey-er is fine, but not without any trade-offs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same effect in my games, but I gave Crinos 1 more point of Stamina. It's how the math worked out when I had &quot;re-balanced&quot; all of the war forms. I gave the war forms 9 dots of attributes and the near war forms (in this case Hispo) 8 dots. From memory, I think the Bastet and Rokea worked out slightly differently since their primary war form is the near animal forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T12:11:55-07:00","id":640509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=640014#post640014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the speed, bulk and athletics,if you're fighting with Fangs and Teeth, Hispo is the mathematically better choice then Crinos!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me, I find the werewolf in <i>An American Werewolf in London</i> more terrifying than any of the semi-bipedal ones I've seen in other media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T15:09:44-07:00","id":640686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=640327#post640327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same effect in my games, but I gave Crinos 1 more point of Stamina. It's how the math worked out when I had &quot;re-balanced&quot; all of the war forms. I gave the war forms 9 dots of attributes and the near war forms (in this case Hispo) 8 dots. From memory, I think the Bastet and Rokea worked out slightly differently since their primary war form is the near animal forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the Hispo and Lupus equivalents for Rokea are only available when they're immersed in a fairly sizable body of salt water. At least, since they got rid of the hilarious on-land Dexterity penalty for Chasmus. It's like they predicted how weird Jaws: Unleashed would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T15:38:28-07:00","id":640713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=640686#post640686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the Hispo and Lupus equivalents for Rokea are only available when they're immersed in a fairly sizable body of salt water. At least, since they got rid of the hilarious on-land Dexterity penalty for Chasmus. It's like they predicted how weird Jaws: Unleashed would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I remember being so confused by Chasmus having a dex penalty on land, and not just saying it shouldn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T16:09:46-07:00","id":640769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=640713#post640713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, I remember being so confused by Chasmus having a dex penalty on land, and not just saying it shouldn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even more hilariously, <i>Chasmus was less ungainly on land than Crinos</i>. This lasted from the time that the second edition player's guide was released up until the breedbook, from spring 1998 to spring 2001. It was even reprinted in Hengeyokai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T17:16:46-07:00","id":640835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=638790#post638790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breed form is out because it's silver-safe, unless you're the breed that should formerly have been known* as metis.<br /> <br /> Some Gifts are actually keyed to work only in certain forms. Ancestral Wings is a Hispo-only affair, for example. You could build on themes along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont agree because i still think that then whole &quot;you can regenerate in breed form but dont take damage from silver in it&quot; rule to be silly. I still think that werewolf should take damage from silver and regenerate in all forms, more streamlines and i havent seen anything in the setting that would stop working because of that change to be honest.<br /> <br /> On the forms things i guess its an agree to disagree kinda thing, i still feel that form should be give something more of what they have right now besides stats (Which only difference is swapping 1 point of strenght for dex)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:00:11-07:00","id":640851,"title":"","content":"I saw the white howlers drawings and did not like the art of that book See HQ of Conan can help, W 20 art is great...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3958-silverb","name":"Silverb","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3958_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:27:53-07:00","id":640878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=640835#post640835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the forms things i guess its an agree to disagree kinda thing, i still feel that form should be give something more of what they have right now besides stats (Which only difference is swapping 1 point of strenght for dex)</div> </div> </div> </div>They also have different speeds, and jumping ability, and opposable thumbs.<br /> Oh, and Crinos aren't good with talking, but I don't believe Hispo can at all. I have also played with Hispo having slightly heightened senses (-1 dif instead of Lupus' -2).<br /> <br /> In any case, I can see why you think that Hispo and Crinos aren't diverse enough. It's just not something that has ever bothered me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T19:53:27-07:00","id":641010,"title":"","content":"Hispo can talk, but it takes a lot of effort (one Willpower to say what Crinos normally manages, nothing beyond that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=640835#post640835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont agree because i still think that then whole &quot;you can regenerate in breed form but dont take damage from silver in it&quot; rule to be silly. I still think that werewolf should take damage from silver and regenerate in all forms, more streamlines and i havent seen anything in the setting that would stop working because of that change to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means that the slightest contact with silver or any injury become severe veil breaches, so it probably wouldn't work too well. These monsters need to hide, or at least appear human or wolf enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T22:22:23-07:00","id":641137,"title":"","content":"A lot of the changes suggested sound like things from forsaken. <br /> <br /> Perhaps convert apocalypse into the forsaken rules? Second edition mind you. Not that I'm trying to dissuade change, but I think that'll make people happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T00:14:23-07:00","id":641248,"title":"","content":"No, using nWoD rules won't make people happy, the Translation Guide is just for that.<br /> <br /> The first rule for the 4th edition is to not be nWoD, even if taking a little from there. That's valid for all 4th editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T05:52:45-07:00","id":641429,"title":"","content":"Its not about changing the system to NWoD but forsaken 2ed has <b><u>some</u></b> good ideas that could be use in Apocalypse 4th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:17:33-07:00","id":642010,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd love for fourth edition would be actually compatible systems. Pick one set of rules (particularly combat rules) and stick with them, only adding on that which is appropriate for the supernatural aspects of particular creatures. Something that gives dice bonuses in one game shouldn't lower difficulties in another and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:17:45-07:00","id":642138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=642010#post642010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'd love for fourth edition would be actually compatible systems. Pick one set of rules (particularly combat rules) and stick with them, only adding on that which is appropriate for the supernatural aspects of particular creatures. Something that gives dice bonuses in one game shouldn't lower difficulties in another and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this. There should not be different defense options depending on the game being played. It makes it harder to switch between playing different games when the basic rules vary.<br /> Also, if multiple actions are going to continue being a thing, decide on a fair system to go by and don't change it in every book and edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T15:38:47-07:00","id":643473,"title":"","content":"I think you misunderstood me, I was suggesting the translation guide to people wantin such changes, NOT saying it's somethinf onyx path should adopt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T17:13:33-07:00","id":643565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=642010#post642010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'd love for fourth edition would be actually compatible systems. Pick one set of rules (particularly combat rules) and stick with them, only adding on that which is appropriate for the supernatural aspects of particular creatures. Something that gives dice bonuses in one game shouldn't lower difficulties in another and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look the other pages of the thread you'll find this being asked on most of them.<br /> <br /> Yeah, for the sake of all that's nerdy, please make a common system instead of reinventing the wheel every freaking time again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T22:14:16-07:00","id":643761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=643565#post643565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look the other pages of the thread you'll find this being asked on most of them.<br /> <br /> Yeah, for the sake of all that's nerdy, please make a common system instead of reinventing the wheel every freaking time again.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can put it to the tune of an ancient meme.<br /> <br /> ALL YOUR BASE YOUR BASE YOUR BASE<br /> ALL YOUR BASE SYSTEM<br /> SHOULD BE CROSS-COMPATIBLE","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T10:50:56-07:00","id":644412,"title":"","content":"How different is it currently, between games? I've only done apocalypse for Cwod, but for nwod I've done vamp and werewolf and noticed they had similar systems all around. Never occurred to me that classic world would be radically different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T11:50:42-07:00","id":644455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=644412#post644412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How different is it currently, between games? I've only done apocalypse for Cwod, but for nwod I've done vamp and werewolf and noticed they had similar systems all around. Never occurred to me that classic world would be radically different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Abilities end up being far out of focus in other games, like how Werewolf doesn't bother with Finance and seems to have purged Politics completely in W20. Vampire also lacks Enigmas. M20, meanwhile, has Technology as a Skill instead of as a Knowledge. Thus far for the Anniversary editions, only M20 thought that having a separate Martial Arts Ability was a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:27:05-07:00","id":644583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/620572-4th-edition-changes?p=644412#post644412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How different is it currently, between games? I've only done apocalypse for Cwod, but for nwod I've done vamp and werewolf and noticed they had similar systems all around. Never occurred to me that classic world would be radically different.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how in nWoD they have that neat blue book called World of Darkness, with all the core rules in it? How even with Second Edition copying those rules (updated by GMC), they just copy the main rules? And how they even have some common rules covering all the powers, like the rule on Clash of Wills?<br /> <br /> So, how to put this? In cWoD we don't have NOTHING like it whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Each book basically have its own rules. And by that I mean, its own rules, really. They only share most (not all) of the sheet and the premise of rolling Att+Hab against set dif. Every other thing in the book will be different in each core. They change initiative systems, grapple rules, everything.<br /> <br /> They are proud of traits that don't exist in the other books. You know how a lot of Gifts use the target Permanent Rage as dif? well, no other splat have Rage whatsoever. Actually, most don't have ANYTHING mechanically resembling Rage. Heck, not even the rules to create a mortal sheet are the same. What if a mortal runs into something scary? In Vampire the mortal rolls Courage. In Mage Courage isn't even a thing.<br /> <br /> Hell, the inconsistencies from one system to the other are, seriously, everywhere. Simply because in the end they are distinct systems. There are no cWoD Storyteller System. There is a system for each and every game line, none of them bound to follow the others. They simply never wanted to cross-compatible. Even sharing the same &quot;base&quot; system and, arguably, the same setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:48:08-07:00","id":644604,"title":"","content":"Well i dont fault the other splats for not having &quot;rage&quot; as that is a Werewolf centric thing, same a courage/etc is vamps only (i think). The same thing do tend to happen in NWoD with each splat having supernatural advantage and those working slightly different in place.<br /> <br /> But while system wise it seems they dont support other line, fluff wise is way more supported than NWoD.<br /> <br /> That said thing like multiaction rules are different between splats. Mage revised and DA:20 having the good set in them while other dont.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:56:29-07:00","id":644611,"title":"","content":"Rage is one of the easier stats to fudge an equivalent for, though. (10-Humanity/Path), P'o/permanent Angst, and Torment can all fill in there reasonably well in a thematic sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T02:49:58-07:00","id":645196,"title":"","content":"Sure, fluff-wise the traits make sense, all of them. The problem is the mechanical implications. And, to a lesser degree, the lack of well-thought and clear official answers to the conundrums.<br /> <br /> When a Gift asks the target's Rage, you have options for most splats. But those options already carry problems. 11-Humanity seems good, the same for Torment+1. It is thematically in tune, and at least give you the range between 1 and 10 (Humanity 0 and Torment 10 aren't meant to be playable, so I use the +1 on both to correct the math). But they are also far less fluid, given their role and starting points. Changelings and Mages, though, are far harder to accommodate. Rage is Glamour or Banality? Arete can easily be used as a catch-all for &quot;resistance&quot;, but its steady raise make it too hard for starting characters, and too predictable for Archmasters.<br /> <br /> I'm sure they can think of ways to have some compatibility. Enough for us to know what to do during crossovers. If the splats still have such distinct traits (and I DO think some of them could be taken out anyway, to begin with Vampire's Virtues, and maybe with the current mechanic for Rage), at least the answer about what to do in such cases should be made intuitive or clear in the book.<br /> <br /> But since we're at it, anyway. The rules for Clash of Powers stink in a general sense, with Vampire's rules being the worst. Can we have a system of Clash of Powers where you don't instantly loose or win because of XP invested?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}